{"id": "EUVD-2026-102286", "enisaUuid": "087649cf-f694-3fec-92a9-7d509b100fa0", "description": "libewf through 20260924 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libewf_lef_extended_attribute_read_data() because UTF-16 name and value sizes are validated before being doubled. Attackers can supply a crafted .L01/.Lx01 file with oversized 'ea' metadata counts to crash the application or leak uninitialized heap memory through extended attributes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T18:57:47", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libewf-lef-extended-attribute-utf16-size-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libewf/blob/d76fd0bb21601e2969bc88ffdaeb861023f6a5b2/libewf/libewf_lef_extended_attribute.c#L362-L408", "https://github.com/libyal/libewf/blob/d76fd0bb21601e2969bc88ffdaeb861023f6a5b2/libewf/libewf_lef_extended_attribute.c#L456-L560", "https://github.com/libyal/libewf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libewf-through-20260924-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-l01-extended-attribute-parsing"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xjw3-jc7r-r4g6", "CVE-2026-111159"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f997c168-87d1-3469-a59e-14234feeecfb", "product": {"name": "libewf", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260924"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f6c27450-cfa3-3d28-a141-5ddedd11346d", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}